From: Korri RG353M bring-up <noreply@korri.dev>
Subject: [PATCH] allocator: prefer the KMS card before Panfrost render node

On the RG353M, renderD128 is the Panfrost render node. It opens successfully
but cannot service DRM_IOCTL_MODE_CREATE_DUMB, so MPP never reaches card0.
Rockchip DRM card0 provides the dumb-buffer allocator required by MPP.

---
 osal/allocator/allocator_drm.c | 4 ++--
 1 file changed, 2 insertions(+), 2 deletions(-)

--- a/osal/allocator/allocator_drm.c
+++ b/osal/allocator/allocator_drm.c
@@ -52,10 +52,10 @@ typedef struct {
     RK_U32  flags;
 } allocator_ctx_drm;
 
-/* use renderD128 first to avoid GKI kernel permission issue */
+/* card0 is Rockchip DRM; renderD128 is Panfrost on the RG353M. */
 static const char *dev_drm[] = {
-    "/dev/dri/renderD128",
     "/dev/dri/card0",
+    "/dev/dri/renderD128",
 };
 
 static RK_U32 to_rockchip_gem_mem_flag(RK_U32 flags)
